  "result": "I fixed the bug: `click.IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True).convert('0', None, None)` now returns 1 instead of -1. `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` gives 45 passed, 2 skipped.\n\n**Fix:** In `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`, I changed `bound - dir` to `bound + dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` when clamping up to `min` and `dir=-1` when clamping down to `max`, so an open bound has to step by `+dir`. The old code stepped the wrong way for both bounds.\n\n**Tests:** I added four cases to the `test_range` clamp parametrize list at the top of `tests/test_types.py`:\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` converts `\"0\"` to 1.\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` converts `\"-5\"` to 1.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` converts `\"5\"` to 4.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` converts `\"9\"` to 4.\n\nI didn't run the new cases against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
